From a gameplay perspective, the Epilogue is mainly a long series of cutscenes, with some sequence triggers thrown in. 
Here's the quickest way of getting it over with.

== Cloudsgate Citadel ==

Leave.

== Somnia ==

Go up to the throne room, talk to Captain Blade, then leave.

== Sorceria ==

Leave.

== Weaver's Peak ==

Talk to Tania in the upper-left house, then leave.

== Madame Luca's ==

Leave.

== Port Haven ==

Leave.

== Ghent ==

Leave.

== Felonia ==

Leave.

== Weaver's Peak ==

Leave.

== Somnia ==

Go up to the throne room, then talk to Ashlynn (she should be semi-transparent).

== Credits ==

[[File:DQ6 Liquid Metal Mind Scroll.png|thumb|right|Search the spot marked by the blue light for the Liquid Metal Mind scroll!]]

Watch for when Terry shows up (it happens after Milly's scene), and pay careful attention to when a blue light shows up on the ground.  That spot has the Liquid Metal Mind scroll!  That's essential for the post-game!

